Description: pvr: raise the compute workgroup limit to 256 invocations
 maxComputeWorkGroupInvocations is a literal 128 with a size of
 (128, 128, 64), while the driver already handles larger workgroups: sizes
 above 32 invocations are padded to whole tasks
 (pvr_compute_flat_pad_workgroup_size()), barriers across tasks are lowered
 to the shared memory counter in usclib_barrier() (pco_nir_sync.c), the
 register allocator limits temporaries per slot for such workgroups
 (rogue_max_wg_temps()) and spills beyond that, and the CDM workgroup size
 fields take up to 512 per dimension. rogue_get_compute_max_work_group_size()
 returns 512 on cores with ERN 35421 such as BXM-4-64, and the unused
 max_compute_work_group_invocations in pvr_physical_device.c computes 512 for
 its 64 USC slots. Applications such as wgpu programs with
 workgroup_size(256) fail on 128.
 .
 Report 256 invocations, a size of (256, 256, 64) and 8 subgroups per
 workgroup. A barrier in a workgroup of 256 needs 8 of the 64 USC slots at
 the same time. This needs the fix "pco: fence before mutex release ops"
 (patch 0003 in this series), which keeps shared memory writes in barriers.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
